atus": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["audio_transcription"], "text": " Okay, so then this is the final question here, and I'll jump in the pool and stop aggravating you. Is, so basically the beauty of this, right? When we turn the Revel 8 on, we don't need Outlook. We don't need- we don't need any kind of form of business tool. We are just making one shell and wrapper and and node with the APK. And all it is to me is a bunch of fucking data That's gonna get compiled and sent where we need it", "text_chars": 426, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": true, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "54a47781-1061-46f6-b7ba-a27194a8ff52", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790289028.162881, "updated_at": 1790289029.060641, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["audio_transcription"], "text": " Right. The endgame is frictionless intent. But for now, just get a clean shell, solid loop, tight handoffs. Morning, night, like you said. That discipline is what makes the magic feel real.", "text_chars": 190, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": true, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "1dbca073-542c-4b8a-9d14-bd3e21173760", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790289064.9404554, "updated_at": 1790289078.240089, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["audio_transcription"], "text": " Okay", "text_chars": 5, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": true, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "