77.473401, "updated_at": 1790289078.240318, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["audio_transcription"], "text": " Mm-hmm. Yep. The key is the shell owns the workflow so you can swap providers anytime without rewiring your brain.", "text_chars": 115, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": true, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "da6e7ccf-a43c-4dca-8e77-82a5d97dd935", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790289142.3744671, "updated_at": 1790289222.030681, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["audio_transcription"], "text": " Oh I am, am. But I- again, yes. So no, no, no. for-proton family no one utilizes because no one in my family no one cares about security, no one understands- I had to teach my wife about a VPN, right? Proton I have Proton I have because it's my storage and because I was moving to this point of basically Okay, I need a VPN when I travel, right? I need a VPN for a lot of reasons, right? Then yeah- then on top of that, I'd like to secure- I like- I-I-I- I've had enough of Outlook and- and just Outlook overall, Microsoft. Had enough of Google. Right? It- the price you pay for a real business stack for those people is not worth what they do Microsoft Outlook is one of the worst email clients I've ever dealt with. It's gone so backwards, it's fucking crazy. Google Drive, Google, I don't know what it is. It's just It's too UI interfaced. It's not it's too We've gotten to a point where my technical skills and what I need have surpassed what Microsoft can over- give to the general public Makes sense", "text_chars": 1006, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": true, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextract