kinds": ["audio_transcription"], "text": " I hear that. Yeah. Like, you're not crazy. Outlook and Google optimize for the average case, not for what you're trying to do. The move isn't to go off-grid overnight. It's to pick one coherent work family and segment it. Proton for", "text_chars": 233, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": true, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "0a7119e1-2e58-41d7-bcd8-98229e1316ea", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790289280.3608503, "updated_at": 1790289344.866166, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["audio_transcription"], "text": " Well, I- uh- but all's I did with calendar automation was basically that was a good call, good call for calendar automation. What I did is I don't know what I use. I use something and just shared the calendar on Proton. Proton was like my main calendar on my phone. Right, so we-we found the gap, but this is the shit I don't want to do Because then it just turns into five different sprawl layers. I'm sharing a thing here, you're getting it from there. Security here, security there. Two factor auth- you know, all that bullshit", "text_chars": 531, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": true, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "bc6b2e54-6ec9-4819-9d21-3c712a2a22d9", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790289281.450902, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["audio_transcription"], "text": " Lemme check.", "text_chars": 13, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": true, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextracta