rly, not kind of scrape", "text_chars": 275, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": true, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "ff68b1fc-1347-44da-9415-ec2cfa324400", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790289341.501979, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["audio_transcription"], "text": " Right now, we just prove one clean", "text_chars": 35, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": true, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "61e0ac42-ccd7-46ec-8a79-f18ecc999304", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790289342.714345, "updated_at": 1790289344.866378, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["audio_transcription"], "text": " Yeah, so that sprawl is exactly what we're trying to kill. Like rule of thumb, no core function depends on screen scraping or pretending to be human. We use only official APIs, CLIs, or documented local protocols. If a piece doesn't have one, we either leave it manual for now or we pick a service that does. And hey, long term, AG Suit should be the only interface you touch, not Proton, not Google, not Outlook. They become swappable plumbing.", "text_chars": 446, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": true, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "6313614c-1eb2-4455-a288-f7f40fbc01a4", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790289344.4494824, "updated_at": 1790289399.1857, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["audio_transcription"], "text": " Yeah. That-makes- a lot, a lot of sense. That makes a lot-a-lot of sense, right? Because That's the biggest thing because also another thing that I get annoyed about is And I didn't set it up right with the-vari- with the the envelopes and the variables and everything when I started to do all these APIs and and CLIs. But what drives me fucking nuts is all these people have- Some of them have CLI, some of them don't. You got a connector API? I know MCP Oh, we don't have an MCP, you only get this permission You see what I'm saying", "text_chars": 535, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": true, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "80074654-c1f2-424e-9b4a-70f11112a7a6", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790289396.8966568, "updated_at": 1790289415.83012, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["audio_transcription"], "text": " Okay Okay, cool, cool, cool. Drop an anchor commit here. That's what I want to understand. Good work", "text_chars": 101, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": true, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "d73862d4-00f7-42b4-bbb5-3301a06855a0", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790289398.111713, "updated_at": 1790289399.18602, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["audio_transcription"], "text": " Right. Yeah. That asymmetry is real. The way out is to put a thin adapter layer in GCE. One interface we control, many providers underneath. If a provider is messy or hostile to automation, we isolate or replace it. That way, your shell stays stable while the plumbing changes.", "text_chars": 278, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], 