r account, you have to do all this shit. They only give you certain access to certain things This is why I'm pushing back on MCP concept", "text_chars": 627, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": true, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "2fb9e850-4f58-458f-bb8a-58ca17f60ead", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790289503.520716, "updated_at": 1790289504.322082, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["audio_transcription"], "text": " MCP is our normalization layer on top. APIs are the", "text_chars": 52, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": true, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "d087d331-2bc9-467c-bd25-0d62bc2e19c3", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790289561.086085, "updated_at": 1790289582.368263, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["audio_transcription"], "text": " But again, that makes sense. But again, what I'm trying to do is besides the layer you're talking about is build a bridge from whatever provider to basically make my own Outlook or my own calendar", "text_chars": 197, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": true, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "2cdd7caf-ef03-46e2-895f-9a5ede309305", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790289562.423789, "updated_at": 1790289563.769859, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["audio_transcription"], "text": " Hmm. Yeah. Yes. And you're right to push there. MCP doesn't magically grant permissions