 "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "8a0161f3-d844-4a87-8606-849c25406a3a", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790308039.544417, "updated_at": 1790308055.39177, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yeah — I checked it, and **your first impression tracks with what’s showing up publicly**.\n\n**Space Bunny Free / Space Bunny Alpha** just landed in the OpenCode ecosystem. The OpenCode docs describe it as a **stealth model**, free for a limited time, with a provider that follows **zero retention and does not train on your data**. citeturn151463search9\n\nThe interesting bits for what you’re doing:\n\n- It has a **~1M-token context window** and supports reasoning/tool use; one current model listing shows **1,048,576 context** and up to **524,288 output tokens**. citeturn151463search3turn151463search1\n- It’s currently priced at **$0 input / $0 output** in the OpenCode/Zen lane. citeturn151463search3\n- Early users are specifically reporting **fast planning/research** and **multiple sub-agents running in parallel**. One OpenCode community report mentions five sub-agents investigating concurrently and doing it efficiently. citeturn151463reddit44\n- Usage exploded almost immediately: OpenCode’s stats already show thousands of users and hundreds of thousands of completed sessions despite it basically just appearing. citeturn151463search0\n\nAnd here's the part that directly connects to what you just observed: **Space Bunny may be especially suited to the DevPad carousel concept** because it seems happy to decompose work, create its own task structure, and push parallel agent branches without you micromanaging each step. That's exactly what you saw when it spontaneously organized the to-do list and started launching sub-agents.\n\nOne caveat: **its identity is deliberately undisclosed right now.** There’s community speculation that it could be a new MiniMax-family model — someone found tokenizer behavior consistent with MiniMax — but that is *not confirmed*. citeturn151463reddit46turn151463search8\n\nAlso, don't interpret “free sub-agents” as unlimited infrastructure. OpenCode has some current free-tier quirks around which sub-agent types can run and under what session context; there are active issues around free-tier subagent behavior. citeturn151463search4turn151463search6\n\nSo for **your** stack, I wouldn't replace Big Pickle yet. I'd give Space Bunny a very specific job:\n\n> **Carousel candidate / orchestration stress-test model.**\n\nRun the *exact same mature MLB or Voice Bridge lane* through Big Pickle and Space Bunny: same session header, same bootstrap transitions, same stop gates. Measure **role adherence, unauthorized decisions, number of interventions, context retention across bootstrap swaps, sub-agent discipline, and wall-clock time.**\n\nThat will tell us a hell of a lot more than a generic benchmark. Because what you care about isn't “is Space Bunny smart?” It's **“can Space Bunny drive the GCE role carousel without Don babysitting it?”**\n\nAnd based on what I'm seeing, **that's absolutely worth testing.** memcite", "text_chars": 2881, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "cd9ad4e6-19f6-4a68-9eda-285ca40fbe46", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790308058.7379494, "updated_at": 1790308067.863447, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["audio_transcription"], "text": " Hey, so