: "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 1, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "982416b9-7e6a-4443-a45e-b77223e125d1", "role": "tool", "role_name": "web.run", "created_at": 1790311436.438122, "updated_at": 1790311436.438122, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 1, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "32091462-8467-4906-8fe9-074f2ad888ac", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790311436.947473, "updated_at": 1790311436.947473, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "thoughts", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "8d79fb53-6c46-4445-8013-b7aabf1903d0", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790311436.954012, "updated_at": 1790311436.954012, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "47240a62-4d3b-4ac9-9ace-6e701a7503a2", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790311436.956742, "updated_at": 1790311444.596589, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "On current T-Mobile 5G, **roughly 144–561 Mbps down, 6–34 Mbps up, and 15–27 ms latency** is their published typical range for most on-device plans. Hotspot/tethering is typically around **118–402 Mbps down, 6–33 Mbps up, and similar 15–27 ms latency**. citeturn537123search0turn537123search2\n\nFor what **we're doing with OpenCode/Bedrock/model calls**, I'd care less about headline download speed and more about stability: **packet loss near 0%, jitter preferably <20–30 ms, and latency that isn't randomly spiking into the hundreds**.\n\nSo if your test gives you something like **150+ Mbps down / 10+ Mbps up / 20–40 ms ping with basically zero packet loss**, I'd be very comfortable running the DevPad off that. Even **50 Mbps** is plenty if it's rock solid.\n\nIf the hotel Wi-Fi is showing 20 Mbps but dropping packets, **I'd take stable T-Mobile 5G at 50 Mbps all day long.**", "text_chars": 882, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "23e3a1e1-4eff-4042-83ea-cdd91d7a1da2", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790311456.017459, "updated_at": 1790311466.142105, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "You gotta look at that. I was only getting 30. I'll test it right now. Because one second, I'll test my phone on the internet versus the T-Mobile phone. This bullshit about 30 megabytes is horrible.", "text_chars": 198, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "fd7e6480-113e-49fe-9a9c-834b0cf974b2", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790311459.680513, "updated_at": 1790311459.680513, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "7346b747-c4c9-4c08-9a40-27f63e51f75f", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790311459.70515, "updated_at": 1790311465.6556, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yeah—**30 Mbps on T-Mobile 5G is on the weak side**, especially on the Strip, but it’s not automatically unusable if it’s stable.\n\nOne important thing when you test: make sure the app is showing **Mbps**, not **MB/s**.  \n- **30 Mbps** = about **3.75 MB/s**\n- **30 MB/s** = about **240 Mbps**\n\nFor our use case, send me these four numbers from each phone: **download, upload, ping, and jitter/packet loss** if the test gives it. The winner isn’t necessarily the one with the biggest download number—it’s the one with the cleanest connection.", "text_chars": 540, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "4a99e1f7-ce57-4ecb-88c9-b71f1d5183a4", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790311504.227819, "updated_at": 1790311514.430427, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["image_asset_pointer", "text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 1, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["image_asset_pointer"]}, {"message_id": "32b91bed-8e66-4d79-8a35-abaffb56d439", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790311508.302001, "updated_at": 1790311514.182998, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yeah, **that’s much better**.\n\nYou’re getting about **97.7 Mbps down** on **5G UC**. That is absolutely enough bandwidth for OpenCode, Bedrock, API calls, large prompts, syncing files, and the DevPad work we’ve been talking about.\n\nThe only thing that jumps out is the **55 ms ping**. That’s not terrible, but it’s not especially tight either. More importantly, the screenshot shows a loaded latency figure around **156 ms**, which suggests the connection gets noticeably slower under traffic.\n\nSo the takeaway is:\n\n- **97.7 Mbps download:** good\n- **55 ms idle ping:** acceptable\n- **~156 ms loaded latency:** worth watching\n- **5G UC:** you’re on T-Mobile’s faster 5G layer, which is good\n\nFor our use case, I’d take this over a hotel Wi-Fi connection doing 20–30 Mbps **if the hotel network is dropping packets**.\n\nThe next thing I want to see is **upload + packet loss/jitter**. That will tell us whether this is actually a clean DevPad connection or just a fast speed-test number.", "text_chars": 985, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "471a93dd-51dd-4a1f-ba62-abd34cdcb780", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790311558.5503058, "updated_at": 1790311572.131512, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["image_asset_pointer", "text"], "text": "Yeah, this is the internet we've been dealing with in fucking MGM. I'm— I don't know. They're capping the shit out of this.", "text_chars": 123, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["image_asset_pointer"]}, {"message_id": "95006ce4-a735-46e3-9671-8f74ba383099", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790311564.023635, "updated_at": 1790311571.896262, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yeah — **that MGM Wi-Fi is the problem**.\n\nYou’re showing about **19.5 Mbps down**, but the bigger tell is the **8 ms idle ping jumping to ~9 ms loaded** on that snapshot. The raw latency looks fine there, but hotel Wi-Fi can still be awful because of congestion, shaping, roaming between access points, and intermittent packet loss. A speed test can look “okay” while long-running model/API sessions still get hammered.\n\nCompared to the T-Mobile test you showed:\n- **T-Mobile:** ~97.7 Mbps down\n- **MGM Wi-Fi:** ~19.5 Mbps down\n\nThat’s roughly **5× the download throughput** on T-Mobile.\n\nFor normal browsing, 20 Mbps is fine. For our workflow — sustained terminal sessions, streaming model output, multiple concurrent API calls, big context payloads, file sync — I’d rather have the T-Mobile connection even before we measure packet loss.\n\nSo your next move is simple: **hotspot the laptop from the Revel and run the same OpenCode task that was flaky on MGM Wi-Fi.** If the failures disappear, we’ve isolated the transport layer pretty cleanly.\n\nAnd yes, they absolutely *could* be shaping or rate-limiting guest Wi-Fi, but from this screenshot alone we can’t prove deliberate capping. We can prove the hotel connection is materially slower.", "text_chars": 1243, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "3ac99010-149d-4e9f-9d8f-8fe829b8dea6", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790311605.498728, "updated_at": 1790311615.795656, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "The other simple thing before I go to bed. The Revel phone wasn't charged, right? So I had to charge it. It's not taking a full charge. Should I leave it overnight because it's just brand new phone?", "text_chars": 198, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "5984debf-514e-43ec-baad-ac8d7f5f4de8", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790311609.346622, "updated_at": 1790311615.45914, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yeah — **leaving it plugged in overnight once is fine**, especially on a brand-new phone.\n\nA few normal reasons it may not be hitting 100% right away:\n- **Adaptive/optimized charging** may intentionally pause around 80–90%.\n- The phone may still be doing **first-day setup, app updates, indexing, and background sync**.\n- A weak charger/cable can make it charge very slowly.\n- If it got warm, Android may temporarily **throttle charging**.\n\nFor tonight, I’d just use a decent wall charger, leave it plugged in, and check it in the morning. If it still won’t reach full charge after that, then we look at the battery protection settings and charger wattage.\n\nOne thing: **don’t assume the battery itself is bad yet**. Brand-new Androids often behave a little weird the first day while everything settles.", "text_chars": 803, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "33d683e1-388c-4763-9751-f8abcae1fc92", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790313228.8893661, "updated_at": 1790313236.413942, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Space Bunny to the rescue, bro. Space Bunny closing us out tonight.", "text_chars": 67, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "cfd9607c-a4d5-4316-8e98-6a72a0766d57", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790313230.533726, "updated_at": 1790313230.533726, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "model_editable_context", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "2115ce65-63b0-46c9-adbf-9b8613c338e0", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790313231.519794, "updated_at": 1790313231.519794, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "e0d94807-b405-4acc-b6c1-83d04580c354", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790313231.524341, "updated_at": 1790313235.945305, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Hell yeah. **Space Bunny gets the night shift.** 😂\n\nThat actually makes tonight’s lesson pretty clean: the free/stealth model isn’t “the answer,” but it **did exactly what you needed in the moment** — organized, held the lane, pushed the work forward, and helped close instead of creating another seven-hour loop.\n\nSo tomorrow we don’t romanticize it. We **measure it** against the framework and decide where it belongs in the carousel. But for tonight?\n\n**Space Bunny earned a seat at the table.** 🐰", "text_chars": 500, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "ff0dec17-184c-4b60-aeb7-d30b09bb1e89", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790313245.5095859, "updated_at": 1790313254.19991, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "You said it right in the other chat when I said what happened is it was just seat fatigue.", "text_chars": 90, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "4944ba69-0280-4041-8446-4a293b06c396", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790313248.037907, "updated_at": 1790313253.821488, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yeah — **seat fatigue** was exactly the right diagnosis.\n\nWhat happened wasn’t really “the framework failed” or “the model got dumb.” It was that the same seat kept getting asked to re-enter, re-verify, re-contextualize, and re-certify a bunch of tiny adjacent changes across multiple work orders. After enough loops, the role boundary starts to blur and the operator tax explodes.\n\nThat’s why Space Bunny felt so refreshing at the end: **fresh seat, fresh context, narrow closure task.** It wasn’t carrying eight hours of accumulated friction.\n\nThat distinction matters for tomorrow. We should design around **seat fatigue as a first-class failure mode**: rotate or reset seats before context gets mushy, keep work-order boundaries hard, and don’t make Lucci re-certify every paper cut. That’s probably one of the biggest orchestration lessons from today. memcite", "text_chars": 866, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "d41d09c2-56b7-44a5-9961-50bb19134714", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790373964.088172, "updated_at": 1790373972.081003, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["image_asset_pointer", "text"], "text": "How? What a weird coincidence that the lady that helps me at the Excalibur at the front desk is called Luchi.", "text_chars": 109, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["image_asset_pointer"]}, {"message_id": "67ffc042-d61c-4a82-b1df-f8c291c54389", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790373965.455385, "updated_at": 1790373965.455385, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "model_editable_context", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "fb103d7f-5ac3-4754-885b-fae790fa09ff", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790373967.261343, "updated_at": 1790373967.261343, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "78b71cc4-3ed1-4ba4-a20d-04c7819d69d7", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790373967.264574, "updated_at": 1790373971.951263, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "That is a pretty great coincidence. 😂\n\nYou’ve been talking about **Lucci as the overworked verification seat**, and then the actual front-desk person helping you at Excalibur hands you a card with **“Lucine”** written on it — close enough visually and phonetically to make your brain go, *come on, seriously?*\n\nNot mystical evidence of anything, obviously. Just one of those weird pattern-collision moments that lands harder because the name is already living rent-free in your head all day.\n\nAlso, after the amount of seat fatigue you were dealing with, it is objectively funny that “Lucci” apparently followed you into the physical world.", "text_chars": 640, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "34635c63-b32a-4d1c-8340-a23752621f9b", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790373986.449424, "updated_at": 1790373992.914334, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "That is crazy.", "text_chars": 14, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "35c33c69-21a7-426e-bc71-50a052f5d04b", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790373987.979415, "updated_at": 1790373987.979415, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "model_editable_context", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-